 },
 "summary": "A wideband 50 Ω gain block built on an E-pHEMT process, covering 30 to 2000 MHz. Biased through its output pin from +3 V to +5 V, it gives about 21 dB of gain, a 1.2 dB noise figure and +37.4 dBm output IP3 at 1 GHz on a 5 V supply, drawing 141.7 mA typical. It comes in a SOT-89 plastic case (case style DF782) with an exposed paddle that serves as a ground pin. Named uses are base-station infrastructure, CATV and cellular equipment.",
